1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,590
A Yale-educated former Goldman Sachs executive,

2
00:00:03,590 --> 00:00:05,958
his son who joined as the first

3
00:00:05,958 --> 00:00:08,784
hire, a concept car that raised money

4
00:00:08,784 --> 00:00:10,465
to buy metal printers,

5
00:00:10,465 --> 00:00:13,673
and a hypercar that debuted online because

6
00:00:13,673 --> 00:00:15,812
the auto show was cancelled.

7
00:00:15,992 --> 00:00:19,012
That is the story behind the Czinger

8
00:00:19,012 --> 00:00:19,348
21C.

9
00:00:19,528 --> 00:00:21,253
It is not a simple one,

10
00:00:21,253 --> 00:00:24,555
and our sources disagree on several details.

11
00:00:24,735 --> 00:00:26,511
Here is what they actually say.

12
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:30,584
Our sources are an interview-based article from

13
00:00:30,584 --> 00:00:33,356
CSQ in September twenty twenty-two,

14
00:00:33,356 --> 00:00:37,159
an engineering article from the American Society

15
00:00:37,159 --> 00:00:41,516
of Mechanical Engineers dated March twenty twenty-five,

16
00:00:41,516 --> 00:00:42,862
a Facfox history,

17
00:00:42,862 --> 00:00:46,189
GTPlanet's February twenty twenty preview,

18
00:00:46,189 --> 00:00:49,358
a Backfire News report from March twenty

19
00:00:49,358 --> 00:00:51,497
twenty-four, and Wikipedia.

20
00:00:51,677 --> 00:00:53,153
Where they conflict,

21
00:00:53,153 --> 00:00:54,777
we show both versions.

22
00:00:54,957 --> 00:00:57,267
Our own arithmetic is labelled.

23
00:00:57,618 --> 00:00:59,638
Start with Kevin Czinger.

24
00:00:59,818 --> 00:01:01,353
CSQ describes him,

25
00:01:01,353 --> 00:01:03,144
in twenty twenty-two,

26
00:01:03,144 --> 00:01:05,276
as sixty-three years old,

27
00:01:05,276 --> 00:01:07,066
from Cleveland, Ohio,

28
00:01:07,066 --> 00:01:09,199
and based in Los Angeles.

29
00:01:09,379 --> 00:01:11,725
He went to Yale College and Yale

30
00:01:11,725 --> 00:01:14,952
Law School, and later studied engineering at

31
00:01:14,952 --> 00:01:16,786
Arizona State University.

32
00:01:16,966 --> 00:01:19,389
He played football at Yale in the

33
00:01:19,389 --> 00:01:22,546
late nineteen seventies and early eighties,

34
00:01:22,546 --> 00:01:24,748
and his first job was with the

35
00:01:24,748 --> 00:01:27,024
recreation department of Parma,

36
00:01:27,024 --> 00:01:27,391
Ohio.

37
00:01:27,741 --> 00:01:29,347
His business career,

38
00:01:29,347 --> 00:01:30,712
according to CSQ,

39
00:01:30,712 --> 00:01:34,163
included a senior executive role at Goldman

40
00:01:34,163 --> 00:01:38,097
Sachs and multiple high-ranking positions at Coda

41
00:01:38,097 --> 00:01:38,980
Automotive.

42
00:01:39,160 --> 00:01:41,677
The article gives no dates or titles

43
00:01:41,677 --> 00:01:42,446
for either.

44
00:01:42,626 --> 00:01:44,741
It also says he was a founding

45
00:01:44,741 --> 00:01:47,843
funder and board member of Achievement First

46
00:01:47,843 --> 00:01:48,407
Schools.

47
00:01:48,587 --> 00:01:50,685
So by the time he turned to

48
00:01:50,685 --> 00:01:52,705
cars, he had lived in law,

49
00:01:52,705 --> 00:01:55,890
finance, education and the auto industry.

50
00:01:56,240 --> 00:01:58,462
CSQ quotes his view of the car

51
00:01:58,462 --> 00:02:02,757
industry: the current manufacturing system is economically

52
00:02:02,757 --> 00:02:05,276
broken and environmentally broken,

53
00:02:05,276 --> 00:02:07,794
and a new digital system is needed

54
00:02:07,794 --> 00:02:10,090
rather than incremental change.

55
00:02:10,270 --> 00:02:11,977
That is the motive behind the company.

56
00:02:12,157 --> 00:02:13,617
It is a stated belief,

57
00:02:13,617 --> 00:02:15,874
and the article presents it as his

58
00:02:15,874 --> 00:02:18,264
reasoning, not as a measured result.

59
00:02:18,614 --> 00:02:19,937
The car came second.

60
00:02:20,117 --> 00:02:23,330
CSQ says Divergent 3D launched in twenty

61
00:02:23,330 --> 00:02:27,026
fourteen, making cars by three-D printing with

62
00:02:27,026 --> 00:02:28,070
reused metal.

63
00:02:28,250 --> 00:02:30,372
Facfox says it was founded as a

64
00:02:30,372 --> 00:02:32,494
small startup by Kevin Czinger,

65
00:02:32,494 --> 00:02:35,027
and that within its first three years

66
00:02:35,027 --> 00:02:37,149
it had grown into what it calls

67
00:02:37,149 --> 00:02:40,092
an over one hundred million dollar venture.

68
00:02:40,272 --> 00:02:43,560
ASME says Divergent has existed for eight

69
00:02:43,560 --> 00:02:44,603
to ten years.

70
00:02:44,953 --> 00:02:46,392
What did Divergent do?

71
00:02:46,572 --> 00:02:49,979
ASME says its mission is toolless manufacturing

72
00:02:49,979 --> 00:02:52,807
for the primary structures of vehicles.

73
00:02:52,987 --> 00:02:55,566
That means the frame and the major

74
00:02:55,566 --> 00:02:58,903
structural parts, made without the molds and

75
00:02:58,903 --> 00:03:00,951
dies a normal factory uses.

76
00:03:01,131 --> 00:03:04,049
CSQ says the company holds about five

77
00:03:04,049 --> 00:03:05,863
hundred twenty patents,

78
00:03:05,863 --> 00:03:08,387
a figure given by Kevin Czinger.

79
00:03:08,567 --> 00:03:10,971
The sources do not list the patents.

80
00:03:11,320 --> 00:03:13,108
There were early awards.

81
00:03:13,288 --> 00:03:16,270
CSQ says Divergent won the Frost and

82
00:03:16,270 --> 00:03:21,239
Sullivan twenty sixteen North American innovation technology

83
00:03:21,239 --> 00:03:25,297
award, and received moonshot status from Google's

84
00:03:25,297 --> 00:03:26,953
Solve for X program.

85
00:03:27,133 --> 00:03:30,579
It also says the company hired engineers

86
00:03:30,579 --> 00:03:33,078
from SpaceX, Apple and Tesla.

87
00:03:33,258 --> 00:03:35,617
These are the company's own claims as

88
00:03:35,617 --> 00:03:37,147
reported in the article.

89
00:03:37,327 --> 00:03:39,370
The article does not name the people.

90
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:41,102
Money followed.

91
00:03:41,282 --> 00:03:44,752
CSQ quotes Kevin Czinger saying Divergent recently

92
00:03:44,752 --> 00:03:47,598
raised two hundred fifty million dollars,

93
00:03:47,598 --> 00:03:50,929
and that Czinger Vehicles and Divergent together

94
00:03:50,929 --> 00:03:53,844
have raised close to five hundred million.

95
00:03:54,024 --> 00:03:57,262
The article names investors John Thornton,

96
00:03:57,262 --> 00:04:00,037
formerly president of Goldman Sachs,

97
00:04:00,037 --> 00:04:01,193
and Tom Steyer,

98
00:04:01,193 --> 00:04:03,660
the founder of Farallon Capital.

99
00:04:03,840 --> 00:04:05,159
By our arithmetic,

100
00:04:05,159 --> 00:04:08,089
five hundred million over eight years is

101
00:04:08,089 --> 00:04:10,946
about sixty-two million dollars a year.

102
00:04:11,296 --> 00:04:14,134
Lukas Czinger enters the story as the

103
00:04:14,134 --> 00:04:15,208
founder's son.

104
00:04:15,388 --> 00:04:18,221
CSQ says he was twenty-eight in twenty

105
00:04:18,221 --> 00:04:21,725
twenty-two, a former Division One soccer player

106
00:04:21,725 --> 00:04:24,931
who studied electrical engineering at Yale.

107
00:04:25,111 --> 00:04:27,472
He worked at an investment bank in

108
00:04:27,472 --> 00:04:30,873
San Francisco before joining Divergent around age

109
00:04:30,873 --> 00:04:31,776
twenty-three.

110
00:04:31,956 --> 00:04:33,280
By our arithmetic,

111
00:04:33,280 --> 00:04:36,222
that places his arrival about five years

112
00:04:36,222 --> 00:04:37,620
before the article,

113
00:04:37,620 --> 00:04:39,607
so around twenty seventeen.

114
00:04:39,957 --> 00:04:40,978
How did he join?

115
00:04:41,158 --> 00:04:43,345
CSQ says he asked to join after

116
00:04:43,345 --> 00:04:46,025
watching his father present to about a

117
00:04:46,025 --> 00:04:48,635
thousand people at a tech conference.

118
00:04:48,815 --> 00:04:51,952
He was Divergent's first hire after Kevin,

119
00:04:51,952 --> 00:04:55,015
who was then the only full-time employee.

120
00:04:55,195 --> 00:04:57,316
So when we say the company was

121
00:04:57,316 --> 00:04:58,588
a family business,

122
00:04:58,588 --> 00:05:01,134
the sources mean it quite literally:

123
00:05:01,134 --> 00:05:03,679
the second person on payroll was the

124
00:05:03,679 --> 00:05:04,668
founder's son.

125
00:05:05,019 --> 00:05:06,261
His role grew.

126
00:05:06,441 --> 00:05:09,878
CSQ says Lukas assembled and led Divergent's

127
00:05:09,878 --> 00:05:12,846
automation team and holds fifty of the

128
00:05:12,846 --> 00:05:16,205
company's patents, according to his father.

129
00:05:16,385 --> 00:05:17,483
By our arithmetic,

130
00:05:17,483 --> 00:05:19,740
fifty of five hundred twenty is about

131
00:05:19,740 --> 00:05:20,471
ten percent.

132
00:05:20,651 --> 00:05:23,738
ASME in twenty twenty-five lists him as

133
00:05:23,738 --> 00:05:26,665
Founder, President and CEO of the Los

134
00:05:26,665 --> 00:05:29,197
Angeles-based family businesses,

135
00:05:29,197 --> 00:05:31,809
with Kevin as Executive Chairman.

136
00:05:32,159 --> 00:05:35,121
The sources disagree about his title in

137
00:05:35,121 --> 00:05:36,489
twenty twenty-two.

138
00:05:36,669 --> 00:05:39,813
CSQ's body text calls him senior vice

139
00:05:39,813 --> 00:05:43,381
president of operations at Divergent and a

140
00:05:43,381 --> 00:05:46,015
co-founder of Czinger Vehicles.

141
00:05:46,195 --> 00:05:49,100
Its bio box says SVP and CEO

142
00:05:49,100 --> 00:05:51,176
of Czinger Vehicles.

143
00:05:51,356 --> 00:05:52,679
We cannot resolve it.

144
00:05:52,859 --> 00:05:55,278
The simplest reading is that his role

145
00:05:55,278 --> 00:05:59,068
expanded between twenty twenty-two and twenty twenty-five,

146
00:05:59,068 --> 00:06:00,637
but that is our reading,

147
00:06:00,637 --> 00:06:01,683
not a statement.

148
00:06:02,033 --> 00:06:02,985
Now the car.

149
00:06:03,165 --> 00:06:06,506
Facfox says Divergent built a concept called

150
00:06:06,506 --> 00:06:09,316
the Blade, describing it as the first

151
00:06:09,316 --> 00:06:12,278
car with a fully three-D-printed frame.

152
00:06:12,458 --> 00:06:14,498
It says the Blade was used to

153
00:06:14,498 --> 00:06:17,382
raise funds and to acquire metal printers

154
00:06:17,382 --> 00:06:18,718
from SLM Solutions,

155
00:06:18,718 --> 00:06:20,968
and that Jay Leno once drove it.

156
00:06:21,148 --> 00:06:23,883
GTPlanet calls the Blade a proof of

157
00:06:23,883 --> 00:06:26,462
concept for the printing process,

158
00:06:26,462 --> 00:06:28,103
dated twenty fifteen.

159
00:06:28,453 --> 00:06:31,227
GTPlanet gives the Blade's engine as a

160
00:06:31,227 --> 00:06:33,637
two point four litre turbo from a

161
00:06:33,637 --> 00:06:35,682
Mitsubishi Lancer Evolution,

162
00:06:35,682 --> 00:06:38,530
making seven hundred twenty horsepower.

163
00:06:38,710 --> 00:06:40,835
Only GTPlanet says that.

164
00:06:41,015 --> 00:06:44,384
Facfox gives no Blade specifications at all,

165
00:06:44,384 --> 00:06:47,217
and the other sources do not describe

166
00:06:47,217 --> 00:06:47,830
the car.

167
00:06:48,010 --> 00:06:50,536
So the seven hundred twenty figure rests

168
00:06:50,536 --> 00:06:51,799
on a single article,

169
00:06:51,799 --> 00:06:53,315
and we mark it that way.

170
00:06:53,666 --> 00:06:55,601
The link to the 21C is that

171
00:06:55,601 --> 00:06:57,752
the Blade was the predecessor.

172
00:06:57,932 --> 00:07:02,032
Wikipedia's infobox lists the Divergent Blade as

173
00:07:02,032 --> 00:07:03,911
the 21C's predecessor.

174
00:07:04,091 --> 00:07:06,928
Facfox says the structure of the later

175
00:07:06,928 --> 00:07:09,989
car needs no tooling for part manufacture

176
00:07:09,989 --> 00:07:13,124
or assembly, which is the article's claim.

177
00:07:13,304 --> 00:07:16,334
What none of our sources explains is

178
00:07:16,334 --> 00:07:19,617
how the Blade's design evolved into the

179
00:07:19,617 --> 00:07:21,721
21C in engineering terms.

180
00:07:22,072 --> 00:07:24,428
The machines matter in this story.

181
00:07:24,608 --> 00:07:28,559
Facfox says Divergent entered a joint development

182
00:07:28,559 --> 00:07:32,670
partnership with SLM Solutions in twenty seventeen,

183
00:07:32,670 --> 00:07:36,782
aimed at a next-generation multi-laser machine that

184
00:07:36,782 --> 00:07:39,040
became the twelve-laser NXG.

185
00:07:39,220 --> 00:07:40,722
In twenty nineteen,

186
00:07:40,722 --> 00:07:44,914
it says, Divergent bought five pre-production systems

187
00:07:44,914 --> 00:07:46,812
for factory integration.

188
00:07:46,992 --> 00:07:50,231
Parts for suspension and chassis were made

189
00:07:50,231 --> 00:07:54,318
on commercially available SLM eight hundred machines.

190
00:07:54,669 --> 00:07:55,969
In twenty twenty,

191
00:07:55,969 --> 00:07:59,716
Facfox says, Divergent began series production of

192
00:07:59,716 --> 00:08:03,846
safety-critical structures for carmakers in the United

193
00:08:03,846 --> 00:08:05,223
States and Europe,

194
00:08:05,223 --> 00:08:09,047
and planned to run twenty next-generation printing

195
00:08:09,047 --> 00:08:10,806
systems at its factory.

196
00:08:10,986 --> 00:08:12,821
It does not name the carmakers.

197
00:08:13,001 --> 00:08:15,841
ASME later says McLaren and Bugatti have

198
00:08:15,841 --> 00:08:17,900
begun working with Divergent.

199
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:20,549
So the company was supplying parts to

200
00:08:20,549 --> 00:08:22,817
others while it built its own car.

201
00:08:23,167 --> 00:08:24,496
By our arithmetic,

202
00:08:24,496 --> 00:08:26,122
the chain of dates is:

203
00:08:26,122 --> 00:08:28,781
the partnership in twenty seventeen,

204
00:08:28,781 --> 00:08:31,736
the machine purchase in twenty nineteen,

205
00:08:31,736 --> 00:08:34,617
the series production in twenty twenty,

206
00:08:34,617 --> 00:08:37,499
and the car's unveiling in March twenty

207
00:08:37,499 --> 00:08:38,016
twenty.

208
00:08:38,196 --> 00:08:40,479
So the 21C was not the start

209
00:08:40,479 --> 00:08:41,621
of the effort.

210
00:08:41,801 --> 00:08:44,039
It came after about six years of

211
00:08:44,039 --> 00:08:46,906
company building, if we count from twenty

212
00:08:46,906 --> 00:08:47,536
fourteen.

213
00:08:47,886 --> 00:08:51,009
When was Czinger Vehicles itself founded?

214
00:08:51,189 --> 00:08:52,768
Sources disagree.

215
00:08:52,948 --> 00:08:55,759
CSQ and ASME say twenty nineteen,

216
00:08:55,759 --> 00:08:58,996
with ASME saying Kevin founded it with

217
00:08:58,996 --> 00:09:00,273
his son, Lukas.

218
00:09:00,453 --> 00:09:03,546
Facfox says it was founded in twenty

219
00:09:03,546 --> 00:09:06,466
twenty in Los Angeles to build its

220
00:09:06,466 --> 00:09:08,613
first production vehicle,

221
00:09:08,613 --> 00:09:09,300
the 21C.

222
00:09:09,480 --> 00:09:12,545
Wikipedia's page gives no founding date.

223
00:09:12,725 --> 00:09:15,600
We therefore show twenty nineteen and twenty

224
00:09:15,600 --> 00:09:16,057
twenty.

225
00:09:16,408 --> 00:09:19,373
The design is credited on Wikipedia to

226
00:09:19,373 --> 00:09:20,622
David O'Connell.

227
00:09:20,802 --> 00:09:23,469
The page lists the car's designer in

228
00:09:23,469 --> 00:09:26,061
the infobox and does not elaborate.

229
00:09:26,241 --> 00:09:29,349
CSQ says Czinger Vehicles will stay in

230
00:09:29,349 --> 00:09:32,947
performance luxury, and had fewer than fifty

231
00:09:32,947 --> 00:09:33,765
employees.

232
00:09:33,945 --> 00:09:35,609
The Chief Engineer,

233
00:09:35,609 --> 00:09:37,799
per ASME, is Ewan Baldry.

234
00:09:37,979 --> 00:09:40,359
Those are the named people our sources

235
00:09:40,359 --> 00:09:40,673
give.

236
00:09:41,023 --> 00:09:43,170
The car's layout was a statement.

237
00:09:43,350 --> 00:09:45,939
Wikipedia says the driver sits in the

238
00:09:45,939 --> 00:09:48,737
centre with a passenger directly behind.

239
00:09:48,917 --> 00:09:51,525
FastCar says the layout is like the

240
00:09:51,525 --> 00:09:54,579
McLaren F1's and that Czinger gave weight

241
00:09:54,579 --> 00:09:57,857
distribution and performance as the reasons.

242
00:09:58,037 --> 00:10:00,042
The central seat is a nod to

243
00:10:00,042 --> 00:10:02,764
the most famous central-seat road car,

244
00:10:02,764 --> 00:10:04,984
but no source says that was the

245
00:10:04,984 --> 00:10:05,700
intention.

246
00:10:06,050 --> 00:10:09,336
GTPlanet's February twenty twenty preview said the

247
00:10:09,336 --> 00:10:11,636
car would be revealed at the Geneva

248
00:10:11,636 --> 00:10:13,805
Motor Show on the third of March.

249
00:10:13,985 --> 00:10:15,169
That did not happen.

250
00:10:15,349 --> 00:10:18,875
Wikipedia says the Geneva show was cancelled

251
00:10:18,875 --> 00:10:20,798
because of the pandemic,

252
00:10:20,798 --> 00:10:23,362
and that the 21C was unveiled on

253
00:10:23,362 --> 00:10:26,407
the eleventh of March twenty twenty in

254
00:10:26,407 --> 00:10:27,609
London instead.

255
00:10:27,789 --> 00:10:29,011
By our arithmetic,

256
00:10:29,011 --> 00:10:31,455
that is eight days after the planned

257
00:10:31,455 --> 00:10:31,795
date.

258
00:10:32,145 --> 00:10:35,205
Backfire News adds that the car's public

259
00:10:35,205 --> 00:10:38,190
unveiling had also been planned for the

260
00:10:38,190 --> 00:10:40,256
Goodwood Festival of Speed,

261
00:10:40,256 --> 00:10:42,934
and that both were postponed due to

262
00:10:42,934 --> 00:10:43,929
the pandemic.

263
00:10:44,109 --> 00:10:46,407
So the debut the company planned,

264
00:10:46,407 --> 00:10:48,846
at the world's biggest car shows in

265
00:10:48,846 --> 00:10:51,562
the spring and summer of twenty twenty,

266
00:10:51,562 --> 00:10:53,373
never happened as planned.

267
00:10:53,553 --> 00:10:55,500
The sources do not say how the

268
00:10:55,500 --> 00:10:57,187
London unveiling was held.

269
00:10:57,538 --> 00:10:59,337
The early claims were bold.

270
00:10:59,517 --> 00:11:02,675
GTPlanet's preview said a top speed of

271
00:11:02,675 --> 00:11:05,834
two hundred sixty-eight miles an hour,

272
00:11:05,834 --> 00:11:08,493
zero to sixty in one point eight

273
00:11:08,493 --> 00:11:12,566
seconds, over nine hundred thirty horsepower from

274
00:11:12,566 --> 00:11:15,225
the V8, and a 1+1 tandem layout.

275
00:11:15,405 --> 00:11:17,426
It said the price was unconfirmed.

276
00:11:17,606 --> 00:11:21,024
FastCar later reported Czinger's own claim of

277
00:11:21,024 --> 00:11:22,772
two hundred eighty-one.

278
00:11:22,952 --> 00:11:25,189
